17592186431885 1077 "selection" 13194139534668 17592186045417 true] [17592186431885 1078 #edb/ref 17592186431874 13194139534668 17592186045417 true] [17592186431885 1079 #uuid "11f2b70f-bcb2-5554-a4f5-52982774bf66" 13194139534668 17592186045417 true] [17592186431886 1075 #edb/ref 17592186431866 13194139534668 17592186045417 true] [17592186431886 1075 #edb/ref 17592186431875 13194139534668 17592186045417 true] [17592186431886 1075 #edb/ref 17592186431878 13194139534668 17592186045417 true] [17592186431886 1075 #edb/ref 17592186431880 13194139534668 17592186045417 true] [17592186431886 1075 #edb/ref 17592186431882 13194139534668 17592186045417 true] [17592186431886 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534668 17592186045417 true] [17592186431886 1077 "selection" 13194139534668 17592186045417 true] [17592186431886 1078 #edb/ref 17592186431882 13194139534668 17592186045417 true] [17592186431886 1079 #uuid "15f03df0-1c1a-500e-83f5-21bfe8839deb" 13194139534668 17592186045417 true] [17592186431887 1075 #edb/ref 17592186431865 13194139534668 17592186045417 true] [17592186431887 1075 #edb/ref 17592186431868 13194139534668 17592186045417 true] [17592186431887 1075 #edb/ref 17592186431872 13194139534668 17592186045417 true] [17592186431887 1075 #edb/ref 17592186431881 13194139534668 17592186045417 true] [17592186431887 1075 #edb/ref 17592186431884 13194139534668 17592186045417 true] [17592186431887 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534668 17592186045417 true] [17592186431887 1077 "selection" 13194139534668 17592186045417 true] [17592186431887 1078 #edb/ref 17592186431881 13194139534668 17592186045417 true] [17592186431887 1079 #uuid "819f1de9-2d6b-59f9-9ce0-5429b3d56920" 13194139534668 17592186045417 true] [17592186431888 1068 #edb/ref 17592186431886 13194139534668 17592186045417 true] [17592186431888 1069 "q-335383" 13194139534668 17592186045417 true] [17592186431888 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534668 17592186045417 true] [17592186431888 1071 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=4x(t)-{y}^{2}(t)+5y(t)-12 \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)={x}^{2}(t)-4x(t)+2y(t)+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of ODEs above. An equilibrium point of the system is $[2,\\,1]^{T}.$ Which of the following is the system obtained by shifting this equilibrium to the origin?" 13194139534668 17592186045417 true] [17592186431888 1072 #uuid "13f56d3d-b69f-5f92-a641-c6c370a1ed21" 13194139534668 17592186045417 true] [17592186431888 1074 "To shift the system's equilibrium from ${x}^{∗}$ to the origin, we define the deviation vector\n\n$$\nu=x-{x}^{∗},\n$$\n\nwhere $x=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]$ and $u=[\\begin{aligned}u(t) \\\\ v(t)\\end{aligned}].$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nu=x-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\,⇒\\,x=u+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{and}\\,{x}^{′}={u}^{′}.\n$$\n\nIn coordinate form, this can be written as follows:\n\n$$\nx(t)=u(t)+2,\\,y(t)=v(t)+1,\\,{x}^{′}(t)={u}^{′}(t),\\,{v}^{′}(t)={y}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's now substitute these into the given system.\n\n- Substituting into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =4x(t)-{y}^{2}(t)+5y(t)-12 \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =4(u(t)+2)-(v(t)+1)^{2}+5(v(t)+1)-12 \\\\  & =4u(t)+8-({v}^{2}(t)+2v(t)+1)+5v(t)+5-12 \\\\  & =4u(t)+8-{v}^{2}(t)-2v(t)-1+5v(t)+5-12 \\\\  & =4u(t)-{v}^{2}(t)+3v(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Substituting into the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & ={x}^{2}(t)-4x(t)+2y(t)+2 \\\\ {v}^{′}(t) & =(u(t)+2)^{2}-4(u(t)+2)+2(v(t)+1)+2 \\\\  & =({u}^{2}(t)+4u(t)+4)-4u(t)-8+2v(t)+2+2 \\\\  & ={u}^{2}(t)+4u(t)+4-4u(t)-8+2v(t)+4 \\\\  & ={u}^{2}(t)+2v(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the shifted system is the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)=4u(t)-{v}^{2}(t)+3v(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)={u}^{2}(t)+2v(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534668 17592186045417 true] [17592186431889 1068 #edb/ref 17592186431885 13194139534668 17592186045417 true] [17592186431889 1069 "q-335386" 13194139534668 17592186045417 true] [17592186431889 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534668 17592186045417 true] [17592186431889 1071 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=3x(t)-{y}^{2}(t)+6y(t)-12 \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)={x}^{2}(t)+2x(t)+y(t)-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of ODEs above. An equilibrium point of the system is $[1,\\,3]^{T}.$ Which of the following is the system obtained by shifting this equilibrium to the origin?" 13194139534668 17592186045417 true] [17592186431889 1072 #uuid "a1db4f53-42d8-55c9-8ba8-b7dde90ef735" 13194139534668 17592186045417 true] [17592186431889 1074 "To shift the system’s equilibrium from ${x}^{∗}$ to the origin, we define the deviation vector\n\n$$\nu=x-{x}^{∗},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}],\\,u=[\\begin{aligned}u(t) \\\\ v(t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nu=x-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\,⇒\\,x=u+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{and}\\,{x}^{′}={u}^{′}.\n$$\n\nIn coordinate form, this can be written as follows:\n\n$$\nx(t)=u(t)+1,\\,y(t)=v(t)+3,\\,{x}^{′}(t)={u}^{′}(t),\\,{v}^{′}(t)={y}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's now substitute these into the given system.\n\n- Substituting into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =3x(t)-{y}^{2}(t)+6y(t)-12 \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =3(u(t)+1)-(v(t)+3)^{2}+6(v(t)+3)-12 \\\\  & =3u(t)+3-({v}^{2}(t)+6v(t)+9)+6v(t)+18-12 \\\\  & =3u(t)-{v}^{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Substituting into the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & ={x}^{2}(t)+2x(t)+y(t)-6 \\\\ {v}^{′}(t) & =(u(t)+1)^{2}+2(u(t)+1)+(v(t)+3)-6 \\\\  & =({u}^{2}(t)+2u(t)+1)+2u(t)+2+v(t)+3-6 \\\\  & ={u}^{2}(t)+4u(t)+v(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the shifted system is the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)=3u(t)-{v}^{2}(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)={u}^{2}(t)+4u(t)+v(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534668 17592186045417 true] [17592186431890 1068 #edb/ref 17592186431887 13194139534668 17592186045417 true] [17592186431890 1069 "q-335196" 13194139534668 17592186045417 true] [17592186431890 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534668 17592186045417 true] [17592186431890 1071 "$$\n{x}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}]x+[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of ODEs above. The equilibrium point of the system is $[1,\\,1]^{T}.$ Which of the following is the system obtained by shifting the equilibrium to the origin?" 13194139534668 17592186045417 true] [17592186431890 1072 #uuid "cb1b21bd-521d-5db5-99c4-385125d3ec35" 13194139534668 17592186045417 true] [17592186431890 1074 "To shift the system's equilibrium from ${x}^{∗}$ to the origin, we define the deviation vector\n\n$$\nu=x-{x}^{∗}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nu=x-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\,⇒\\,x=u+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{and}\\,{x}^{′}={u}^{′}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x$ and ${x}^{′}$ into the given system, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}]x+[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}](u+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}])+[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}]u+[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}]u+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}]u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the shifted system is\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}]u.\n$$" 13194139534668 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-0f38395a-e0c9-5a4c-9a38-9a34b59867d5" 17592186431865 "answer-192d2edf-e2b5-5feb-98f3-9b9f0bb71069" 17592186431866 "answer-1b548975-82b4-57b7-b2e8-0a87a8cc8fdf" 17592186431867 "answ